@page "/admin/help"
@layout paa_frontend.Client.Layout.AdminPortalLayout
<div class="help-page"><h1>Administration help centre</h1><p class="lead">Use this guide to manage school information safely and consistently.</p><section><h2>Dashboard and directory</h2><p>The dashboard highlights active learners, recent joins, transfers, staff activity, and items needing attention. The student directory is for finding records, updating profiles, importing learners, and viewing class lists.</p></section><section><h2>Students and staff</h2><p>Search before creating a new record to avoid duplicates. Check names, class, status, and contact details before saving. Use the staff area to manage teacher and bursar accounts according to your school’s process.</p></section><section><h2>Academics</h2><p>Set up classes, subjects, and academic choices before teachers enter marks. Make changes carefully because setup affects what staff can select later.</p></section><section><h2>Marks approval</h2><p>Review the subject, assessment title, term, year, scores, and teacher before approving. Approved marks are what students use for their results. If a report is regenerated, review and approve it again before release.</p></section><section><h2>Reports and analytics</h2><p>Choose the correct term and year. Use report management for official report cards and teacher analytics for patterns across classes and subjects. Treat generated comments as drafts until reviewed.</p></section><section><h2>Safety and support</h2><p>Do not share passwords. Double-check bulk imports and deletions. If a page looks wrong, record the learner, term, year, and action you took before asking for help.</p></section></div><style>.help-page{max-width:900px;margin:32px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#0f172a}.help-page h1{font-size:32px;margin:0 0 8px}.lead{color:#64748b;margin-bottom:26px}.help-page section{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:18px;padding:20px;margin:14px 0;box-shadow:0 4px 14px #0f172a0a}.help-page h2{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 8px}.help-page p{line-height:1.65;color:#475569}</style>
